  "historical_output_text": " Ingredients: ground beef, taco seasoning, diced tomatoes, green bell pepper, onion, flour tortillas, shredded cheese, sour cream, diced avocado, and lettuce. Instructions for cooking: Start by browning the ground beef in a large skillet over medium-high heat until it is no longer pink. Add the taco seasoning and diced tomatoes to the skillet and cook for an additional 5-7 minutes, stirring occasionally. Next, dice the green bell pepper and onion and sauté them in the same skillet until they are soft and tender, about 5 minutes. Layer the cooked ground beef mixture and sautéed vegetables in a baking dish. Sprinkle shredded cheese over the top of the layer and bake the casserole in a preheated 350°F oven for 15-20 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and bubbly.",
